      <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> <span data-year>2026</span></p>

      <p>{{ site.company_name }} ("we", "us", "our") respects your privacy. This notice explains what personal data we collect through this website, why we collect it, how we use it, and the rights you have over it, in line with India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 ("DPDP Act").</p>

      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>{{ site.company_name }} is the "Data Fiduciary" responsible for the personal data described in this notice.</p>
      <p>Registered office: {{ site.address_line1 }}, {{ site.address_line2 }}<br>
      Contact: <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a> · <a href="tel:{{ site.phone_link }}">{{ site.phone_display }}</a></p>

      <h2>2. What personal data we collect</h2>
      <p>When you use our contact form, call us, or message us on WhatsApp, we may collect:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your name and organisation</li>
        <li>Phone number and email address</li>
        <li>Project details you share — sport/surface type, city, plot size, timeline, and any notes</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not knowingly collect sensitive personal data (such as financial, health, or biometric information) through this website.</p>

      <h2>3. Why we collect it</h2>
      <p>We use your personal data only to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Respond to your enquiry and prepare a layout or quote</li>
        <li>Communicate with you about your project, from first contact through handover</li>
        <li>Maintain internal records of enquiries and projects</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not use your data for any purpose beyond what you would reasonably expect from submitting an enquiry, and we do not sell your data to third parties.</p>

      <h2>4. Your consent</h2>
      <p>Where our contact form requires you to tick a consent checkbox, we process your personal data on the basis of that consent. You may withdraw your consent at any time by contacting us at <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a> — this will not affect any processing already carried out before withdrawal, and may affect our ability to respond to an ongoing enquiry.</p>

      <h2>5. How we share your data</h2>
      <p>We do not sell or rent your personal data. We may share it with:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Our own site engineers and project staff, strictly for delivering your project</li>
        <li>Service providers who help us operate this website and respond to enquiries (for example, our website hosting and email delivery providers), who are only permitted to use your data to provide that service to us</li>
        <li>Government or regulatory authorities, where required by law</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>6. How long we keep your data</h2>
      <p>We retain personal data only for as long as necessary to respond to your enquiry, deliver and support any resulting project, and meet our legal or accounting obligations. Data that is no longer needed for these purposes is securely deleted or anonymised.</p>

      <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
      <p>As a Data Principal under the DPDP Act, you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Access the personal data we hold about you</li>
        <li>Request correction or completion of inaccurate or incomplete data</li>
        <li>Request erasure of your personal data, where it is no longer needed for the purpose it was collected</li>
        <li>Withdraw your consent at any time</li>
        <li>Nominate another individual to exercise these rights on your behalf, in the event of your death or incapacity</li>
        <li>Register a grievance with us, and if unresolved, with the Data Protection Board of India</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>8. How to exercise your rights</h2>
      <p>To make any request under this notice, or to raise a grievance about how we handle your personal data, contact us at <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a> or <a href="tel:{{ site.phone_link }}">{{ site.phone_display }}</a>. We will respond within a reasonable time.</p>

      <h2>9. Security</h2>
      <p>We use reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect the personal data we hold from unauthorised access, loss, or misuse.</p>

      <h2>10. Changes to this notice</h2>
      <p>We may update this notice from time to time, including as the DPDP Act's rules are progressively implemented. The "last updated" date above reflects the most recent revision.</p>

      <p style="margin-top:8px;color:var(--grey);font-size:15px">This notice is published voluntarily ahead of the DPDP Act's substantive provisions coming into force, and reflects our current data practices. It is provided for transparency and does not constitute legal advice.</p>
